("SJ3LTXLA","Reciprocity & Justice","Core","Participatory qualitative study using photovoice","International service-learning partnership in Uganda","Hearing and deaf host-community participant-researchers","Centers host-community knowledge and exposes relationship benefits and tensions often omitted from student-focused research.","Participants emphasized friendship, educational relationships, and relationships supporting social change, while also surfacing complex questions about power and the nature of international partnerships.","Findings are context-specific; photovoice participation and publication choices shape which community perspectives are represented.","Require host-community interpretation of outcomes and treat relationships, power, accessibility, and co-authorship as evidence, not background context.",(3,2,2,1,2),"Full-text review",["photovoice","Uganda","host community","international service-learning"]),
